      "snippets": [
        {
          "source_line": 20,
          "tex": "\\noindent\nThe goal of this chapter is to discuss pushouts in the category of\nalgebraic spaces. This can be done with varying assumptions.\nA fairly general pushout construction is given in \\cite{Temkin-Tyomkin}:\none of the morphisms is affine and the other is a closed immersion.\nWe discuss a particular case of this in Section \\ref{section-pushouts}\nwhere we assume one of the morphisms is affine and the other is a\nthickening, a situation that often comes up in deformation theory."
        },
        {
          "source_line": 52,
          "tex": "In Section \\ref{section-compactifications} we use the construction\nof elementary distinguished squares\nin Section \\ref{section-elementary-dsitnguished-squares}\nto prove Nagata's theorem on compactifications in the setting\nof algebraic spaces."
        }
      ],
      "stage_a_readiness": "no_active_candidates"
    },
    {
      "section": 2,
      "kind": "context_only",
      "source_line": 64,
      "snippets": [
        {
          "source_line": 73,
          "tex": "Let $S$ be a scheme and let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$.\nIn this chapter and the following we will write $X \\times_S X$\nfor the product of $X$ with itself (in the category of algebraic\nspaces over $S$), instead of $X \\times X$."
        }
      ],
      "stage_a_readiness": "no_active_candidates"
    },
